SUMMARY:Container Gardening: Supporting Our Local Pollinators in Small Spaces
DESCRIPTION:Pollinators need a supply of nectar throughout the growing season\, so if you are planting up pots for your garden or balcony\, why not choose plants that will attract birds\, bees\, and butterflies? \nThis demonstration\, led by a Toronto Master Gardener\, will start with how to choose soil\, plants\, and containers\, and how to arrange them to maximize their positive impact on the environment. At the end of the demonstration\, materials will be shared with participants\, while supplies last. \nThis program is part of TPL’s Our Fragile Planet program series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter. \nAll are welcome. No registration necessary. \nOptional registration is available for those who wish to receive a reminder email or courtesy phone call prior to the event. Register online\, or by visiting or calling the branch.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/container-gardening-supporting-our-local-pollinators-in-small-spaces/
LOCATION:Danforth Coxwell Library\, 1675 Danforth Avenue\, Toronto\, M4C 5P2
ORGANIZER;CN="Danforth Coxwell Branch%2C Toronto Public Library":MAILTO:dastaff@tpl.ca
END:VEVENT
